{title: 138 - Rise Up, Shepherd, and Follow}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #138 • RISE UP SHEPHERD AND FOL • 11.7.12.7}
{lyricist: American Negro Spiritual}
{composer: Alma Blackmon}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 138}
{meta: tune RISE UP SHEPHERD AND FOL}
{meta: meter 11.7.12.7}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There’s [D/A]a star [Bm]in [G]the [Em]east [A/E]on [F#m]Christmas [G]morn.
[G]Rise [A7/G]up, shepherd, [D/A]and follow.
[G]It will [F#m]lead [Bm]to [A7/G]the place [Cdim]and where [Em/G]the Saviour’s [G]born,
[D/F#]Rise up, [F#m]shepherd, [G]and follow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F#m]Leave your [G]sheep and leave [A7/G]your lamb,
[D/F#]Rise Up, [F#m]shepherd, [A7]and follow.
[Cdim]Leave your ewes [Em/G]and [G]leave [Em]your rams,
[D/F#]Rise Up, shepherd, [F#m]and follow. Follow, Follow,
[F#m]Rise Up, [G]shepherd, and [A7/G]follow.
[D/F#]Follow the [F#m]star of [G]Bethlehem,
[D/F#]Rise Up, shepherd, [Em/G]and [G]follow.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]If you [D/A]take [Bm]goo [G]heed [Em]tothe [F#m]angel's [G]words,
[G]Rise [A7/G]Up, shepherd, [D/A]and follow.
[G]You'll forget [A7/G]your flocks, [Cdim]you'll forget [G]your herds
[D/F#]Rise Up, [F#m]shepherd, [G]and follow.
{end_of_verse}
